<title>KAZAKHSTAN: KAZAKH JULY OIL OUTPUT UP 2.0 PCT M/M TO 2.2 MLN T.</title>
<headline>KAZAKH JULY OIL OUTPUT UP 2.0 PCT M/M TO 2.2 MLN T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan produced 2.21 million tonnes (529,200 barrels per day) of oil and gas condensate in July, up two percent from 2.16 million (518,640 bpd) in June, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical bulletin. Figures in tonnes, except crude oil in million tonnes and natural gas in billion cubic meters.</p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	July	   June	 Jan-July 97</p>
<p> Crude oil		     2.205	  2.161	  14.912</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	+2.0	   -4.5	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     +15.7	  +18.9	   +16.0</p>
<p> Natural gas		   0.641	  0.791	   4.666</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     -19.0	  +59.3	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     +36.2	  +78.3	   +28.4</p>
<p> Gasoline		    165,200	149,000	 988,700</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     +10.9	  +18.2	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -13.9	  -19.5	   -28.9</p>
<p> Diesel			290,500	224,500     1,665,400</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     +29.4	  -27.5	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	-2.3	  -27.1	   -12.7</p>
<p> Fuel oil		    256,200	224,700     1,900,400</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change     +14.0	   -2.4	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change     -11.5	  -24.7	   -12.7</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509 410</p>
</text>
